# A fault kind is a tag `of Fault`, a row kind with no output, and its value is the tag
# itself: `Error(kind=Fs.NotFound, ..)` (Semantics ch. 10, "`~T`, `Error` and `Fault` as a
# row"; doubt FP: "a row kind with no output has values that are its tags"). Applied to an
# argument list it is nothing. prismc's back end refuses it today ("a fault kind
# applied"); the checker should. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject
# to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

Gone: fn Nat -> Error
fn Gone n = Error(kind=Fs.NotFound(), message="gone {n}")

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{(Gone 1).message}")
